  "result": "Perfect! The dashboard feature is complete and all tests pass. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Dashboard Function Summary\n\n### Implementation (src/reports.js):\n\nAdded `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function that returns a comprehensive dashboard with:\n\n1. **counts**: Breakdown of invoices by status\n   - `draft`, `issued`, `partially_paid`, `paid`\n\n2. **outstanding**: Total amount still due\n   - Sum of balanceDue for all `issued` and `partially_paid` invoices\n   - Excludes draft and paid invoices\n\n3. **overdue**: Object with count and amount\n   - Uses `overdueInvoices()` to find past-due invoices\n   - Returns `{ count, amount }` with total due on overdue invoices\n\n4. **topCustomers**: Array of top 3 customers by amount due\n   - Format: `[{ customerId, due }, ...]`\n   - Sorted highest amount first\n   - Only includes `issued` and `partially_paid` invoices\n   - Aggregates multiple invoices per customer\n   - Limited to 3 customers maximum\n\n### Test Coverage (16 comprehensive tests):\n\n- Empty invoice list handling\n- Invoice status counting\n- Outstanding amount calculation (including/excluding statuses)\n- Overdue invoice detection and amount\n- Top customers sorting and aggregation\n- Multiple invoices per customer\n- Limit to 3 customers\n- Data independence validation\n- Edge cases (1, 2, 3 customers)\n\nAll 16 dashboard tests pass \u2705",
